A||||2||Rare87GT||Where to Buy Eibach's and KYB Struts/Shocks||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-23-2001||05:41 AM||||Just looking for a website to find and buy some suspension upgrades for my 87GT.  What would a set of Eibach's cost and the exact drop I would be looking at?  1.5"?  And how much for a set of KYB Struts.  And lastly would this suspension setup be pretty good?  I have heard a lot about caster/camber problems, but I shouldn't have any problems if I get Eibach's and just go and get an alignment will I?  Thanks for the help guys.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-23-2001||09:17 AM||||I've heard the "Tire Rack" has decent prices for Eibachs and KYB's. As for lowering and alignment, I lowered my car 1.5" then took it to a very good alignment shop. They used one of the newer laser machines and dialed in the alignment near perfect. As for adjustment problems, I changed the upper ball joints in the front to the MOOG set. This give full camber and slight caster ajustments. Usually the caster is affected when you change out bushings. Just changing shocks and springs usually only affect toe and camber due to the change in geometry.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||12-23-2001||10:57 AM||||  Try Summit Racing. When I bought mine, you couldn't get them cheaper anywhere else. <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>  <P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
